## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/contactsheet.html
- Summary (EN): The Contact Sheet node arranges its input layers into a grid, similar to a printed contact sheet, also called a mosaic. You control the grid layout, scaling and sampling.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud Contact Sheet dispose les couches d'entrée en grille, comme une planche-contact, avec un contrôle de la disposition, de l'échelle et de l'échantillonnage.

- Inputs meaning: ["image1: a series of layers to arrange into the contact sheet"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: layer type accepted by source", "Images per Line: layers per row before a new row starts", "Stack Vertically: Top to Bottom or Bottom to Top", "Stack Horizontally: Left to Right or Right to Left", "Stack Images in Rows: fills rows first when on, columns first when off", "Max Lines: caps the number of rows; extra layers go to additional outputs", "Keep Full Size: outputs maximum size for the given limits", "Background Color: fill for empty areas", "First Input Offset: shifts the first input position", "Scale Output Resolution: reduces output resolution for quick previews", "Scale Input Images and Scale Input Method: X Axis, Y Axis, or Stretch to Fit", "Clipped Sampling: returns background colour outside a data window", "Filter: sampling method, default Box"]

- Caveats: ["May gain additional outputs if more source images are present", "Full-resolution output can become very large; use Scale Output Resolution"]

